tools: SvLockBytes is exported from the merged library

With --enable-mergelibs SvLockBytes was hidden inside libmergedlo,
yet Calc's libsclo, outside the merged library, uses it. GCC 16
speculatively devirtualizes and emits SvLockBytes's inline destructor
in Calc's objects, which then need the class's vtable and close();
linking libsclo.so failed with undefined references once document.cxx,
documen5.cxx or chartuno.cxx were recompiled (Ely R20.11). The class
is now exported whether or not the libraries are merged, as every
other tools class a module outside the merged library uses.

--- a/include/tools/stream.hxx
+++ b/include/tools/stream.hxx
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@
 to allow UCB to do delayed feeding of data into a SvStream i.e. a kind of a pipe
 mechanism to allow asynchronous fetching of data.
 */
-class UNLESS_MERGELIBS(TOOLS_DLLPUBLIC) SvLockBytes: public SvRefBase
+class TOOLS_DLLPUBLIC SvLockBytes: public SvRefBase
 {
     bool m_bSync;
 
